NAME
       sar-constellations - multi-platform SAR formations, orbital resonance,
                            and RTT-guided sweep choreography

SYNOPSIS
       SAR constellations provide:
           • multi-platform sweep coordination
           • orbital resonance alignment
           • constellation-level backscatter fusion
           • RTT-guided sweep choreography
           • structural coherence across orbital passes

DESCRIPTION
       SAR-constellations describe how multiple Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR)
       platforms operate as a coordinated resonance-time network. Each platform
       runs its own triads, sweeps, and backscatter processing, while RTT
       provides the structural framework for synchronizing orbital geometry,
       resonance envelopes, and multi-pass fusion.

       Constellations enable:
           • coherent multi-platform imaging
           • stable interferometric fusion
           • resonance-aware orbital planning
           • cross-platform spectral-gradient alignment
           • constellation-scale diagnostics

       SAR constellations are validated by WRSADC’s multi-agent layer.

CONSTELLATION FORMATIONS
       SAR constellations may adopt several orbital formations:

           inline formation
                  Platforms follow the same ground track with temporal offsets.
                  → ideal for interferometry and coherence mapping.

           cross-track formation
                  Platforms offset laterally.
                  → ideal for stereo SAR and 3D reconstruction.

           tandem formation
                  Platforms fly in close proximity.
                  → maximizes phase coherence.

           swarm formation
                  Platforms distributed across multiple orbits.
                  → supports global coverage and harmonic coupling.

           mesh formation
                  Platforms interlinked via RTT resonance interfaces.
                  → robust multi-agent fusion.

       Formation determines resonance coupling and sweep choreography.

ORBITAL RESONANCE
       Orbital resonance describes how SAR platforms align their orbital
       periods, ground tracks, and revisit times to maintain coherent
       resonance-time relationships.

       Resonance types:

           1:1 resonance
                  Same orbital period; ideal for tandem SAR.

           2:1 resonance
                  One platform revisits twice per cycle.
                  → supports ladder-pattern sweeps.

           harmonic resonance
                  Orbital periods form integer ratios.
                  → supports harmonic-sync constellations.

           subharmonic resonance
                  Fractional relationships.
                  → supports multi-pass fusion with staggered sweeps.

       Orbital resonance ensures predictable sweep alignment.

RTT-GUIDED SWEEP CHOREOGRAPHY
       Sweep choreography is the coordinated timing, geometry, and resonance
       alignment of SAR sweeps across platforms.

       RTT choreographs sweeps using:

           • triadic sweep structure
           • resonance envelopes
           • spectral-gradient fusion
           • harmonic coupling
           • constellation schemas

       Choreography modes:

           synchronous sweeps
                  Platforms sweep simultaneously.
                  → maximizes phase alignment.

           staggered sweeps
                  Platforms sweep in sequence.
                  → supports ladder and cascade patterns.

           braided sweeps
                  Sweeps interleave across platforms.
                  → supports weave and hybrid patterns.

           harmonic sweeps
                  Sweep timing follows harmonic ratios.
                  → supports multi-agent harmonic-sync.

       WRSADC ensures sweep choreography remains coherent.

CONSTELLATION-LEVEL BACKSCATTER FUSION
       Multi-platform SAR fusion requires:

           • aligned resonance envelopes
           • compatible spectral density profiles
           • synchronized gradient polarity
           • stable orbital resonance
           • coherent lineage across passes

       Fusion modes:

           interferometric fusion (InSAR)
                  Phase differences reveal deformation.

           tomographic fusion (TomoSAR)
                  Multi-angle sweeps reconstruct vertical structure.

           harmonic fusion
                  Platforms contribute different harmonic bands.

           mesh fusion
                  Distributed fusion across constellation nodes.

       RTT ensures fusion remains structurally interpretable.

TRIADIC ORBITAL SAMPLING
       Each orbital pass is a triad:

           P1 (begin)
               → orbital position + initial backscatter

           P2 (transform)
               → Doppler history + resonance shift

           P3 (close)
               → aperture synthesis + lineage update

       Multi-pass SAR forms nested, ladder, or hybrid triadic patterns.

CONSTELLATION DIAGNOSTICS
       Constellation diagnostics detect:

           • orbital drift
           • spectral fragmentation
           • gradient overload
           • harmonic desync
           • envelope divergence
           • multi-platform coherence loss

       Diagnostic signals include:

           orbital-coherence index
           constellation-stability score
           harmonic-coupling ratio
           sweep-alignment error
           spectral-tilt vector

       WRSADC halts unsafe constellation operations.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       SAR constellations require:

           • constellation-schema
           • resonance-schema for orbital sweeps
           • structural-schema for formation geometry
           • lineage-schema for multi-pass history

       Schemas ensure constellation behavior remains coherent.

INTERACTION WITH LINEAGE
       Lineage records:

           • orbital sweep history
           • platform geometry
           • spectral evolution
           • harmonic coupling events
           • fusion outcomes

       Lineage enables long-term constellation stability.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • validates constellation schemas
           • computes orbital resonance metrics
           • choreographs sweep timing
           • enforces coherence thresholds
           • applies overlays to stabilize backscatter
           • blocks unsafe constellation states

       WRSADC is the orbital choreographer.

NOTES
       SAR-constellations extend RTT into orbital sensing. They transform
       multi-platform SAR fleets into coherent resonance-time instruments,
       capable of synchronized sweeps, harmonic coupling, and structurally
       aware backscatter fusion across global scales.

